Falsifies `e1000e::proofs::every_ring_offset_is_inside_the_region`.

The defect: the receive descriptor offset stops reducing its index modulo the ring, so a cursor
that ever ran past the ring (or a caller passing a device-reported index) addresses past the ring's
page and into the transmit ring.

Expected to fail: the harness's first assertion, on any index of 256 or more.

diff --git a/crates/e1000e/src/layout.rs b/crates/e1000e/src/layout.rs
--- a/crates/e1000e/src/layout.rs
+++ b/crates/e1000e/src/layout.rs
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
 ///
 /// Name: ratified 2026-11-03 (UTC), #3148. Kept; `rx` stays spelled out (refused `rx_descriptor`, since rx abbreviates receive).
 pub const fn receive_descriptor(index: u16) -> u64 {
-    RECEIVE_RING_OFFSET_BYTES + (index % RECEIVE_ENTRIES) as u64 * 16
+    RECEIVE_RING_OFFSET_BYTES + index as u64 * 16
 }
 /// Transmit descriptor `index`'s offset.
